 "disclosure": "Go/no-go screen, Amendment 20 (c) as carried by Amendment 21 (e) and its addendum (a); report-only, never evidence. It uses the V11 reference (archived TOPAS F and gain), the V5 reference (TOPAS \u0394IDD and peak/plateau) and the Geant4 thin-target ratios to decide whether the single pre-committed model M2\u2032 is transported at all. It is not a selection among models: M2\u2032 has no free parameter, plan \u00a74.2 forbids switching to M3 on such outcomes, and STOP leads to \"no model change\". It is a stopping rule on gating quantities. The lv5d V11 and V5 runs are therefore not blind to these estimates; they replicate them on independent seeds with the frozen comparators. The M2\u2032 construction outcomes were known before registration (Amendment 21 (a)3) and the de7 record before this addendum; the screen's transport quantities were not. Condition (iv) was revised after de7 to 100 / 150 / 200 MeV and made report-only: its outcome there is predictable from the disclosed construction-level P values. The decisive blind conditions are (i), (i-b), (ii) and (iii). Executed once; recorded whichever way it falls.",
